{
  "purpose": "Ceilings on what the LLM pays per task: the bytes of every JSON response the server returns per budget scenario (max_total_bytes over all calls, max_call_bytes for the largest), the simulated settle and idle waits (max_wait_s: the recorded sleeps of the fake clock, not wall time) and the tools/list the LLM carries every session (instructions, and each default tool description and input schema). Measured through the real server tools on the real captured Chrome trees and the synthetic shapes of CALL_BUDGET.json, so every number is fixture-derived, not a rate on typical pages. Each ceiling is the measured number x 1.1 rounded up; a number changes only with a CE id in changed_by, and that CE records the same number under response_budget (test_budget and test_response_budget check both). Regenerate with python computer_use/call_budget.py --write-response-budget.",
